+Suppose the domains of a collection of partial odometers cover $\Z^2$ and their overlap graph is connected. On each nonempty overlap let $c_{ij}=o_i-o_j$ be constant. There is a function, unique up to an additive constant, compatible with every $o_i$ if and only if the sum of $c_{ij}$ around each finite closed path of the overlap graph is zero.
