+For a field $F$ with $\Delta F\in\{-1,0\}$, choose both inputs at a point with $\Delta F=-1$ and one input at a point with $\Delta F=0$. Call $R$ a \emph{rank} for these choices if it takes values in a totally ordered set and $R(y)<R(x)$ at every chosen input $y\in I(x)$. A nonempty finite forbidden set would have a point of least rank. At that point it must contain at least one input in the first case and both in the second, by Proposition~\ref{prop:recurrence}. In either case it contains a point of smaller rank. Thus a rank on the plane proves recurrence.
