+At a standard child carry the boundary heights on its four polygonal arcs, the ranks for the two signs of the comparison, and the following assertion for each prescribed pair of fields $A,B$ occurring in the chain of translated ancestors. For every $k\in\Z$, $\min(A,B+k)$ is binary superharmonic and recurrent. On the set $A-B=k$, after the inputs off this set have burned, the remaining inputs required for a burn have a decreasing rank periodic in the direction of the band. A site of value $s=1+\Delta F$ burns when $2-s$ of its inputs have burned. The assertion uses the specified positions, slopes and additive constants of the copies.
